      question:"A partially permeable membrane separates a concentrated glucose solution from a dilute glucose solution. State and explain which solution will show a net gain of water molecules.",
      answer:[
        "The dilute solution has a higher concentration of free water molecules (fewer solute molecules per unit volume, so less hydration of water), while the concentrated solution has a lower concentration of free water molecules.",
        "Osmosis moves water from a region of higher water concentration (the dilute solution) to a region of lower water concentration (the concentrated solution), across the partially permeable membrane.",
        "Therefore the concentrated glucose solution will show a net gain of water molecules, while the dilute solution will show a net loss."
      ]
