        "At the microvillus surface, a sodium-dependent glucose cotransporter protein allows Na<sup>+</sup> to re-enter the cell down this concentration gradient; as it does so, the same protein simultaneously carries one glucose molecule into the cell alongside it, even though glucose itself is moving against its own concentration gradient.",
